<div class="doc">
Unfortunately, the coercion loses implicitness of the {x:C'} argument:
  we have to write <span class="inlinecode"></span> <span class="inlinecode"><a class="idref" href="UniMath.SubstitutionSystems.ActionBasedStrengthOnHomsInBicat.html#Instantiation_To_FunctorCategory_And_PointedEndofunctors.Signature_From_ActionBased_Strength.Morphisms.FF"><span class="id" title="variable">FF</span></a></span> <span class="inlinecode"><span class="id" title="var">_</span></span> <span class="inlinecode"><a class="idref" href="UniMath.Semantics.LinearLogic.LinearToLinearNonLinear.html#ConstructionOfComonoidsInEilenbergMoore.xx"><span class="id" title="variable">xx</span></a></span> <span class="inlinecode"></span> instead of just <span class="inlinecode"></span> <span class="inlinecode"><a class="idref" href="UniMath.SubstitutionSystems.ActionBasedStrengthOnHomsInBicat.html#Instantiation_To_FunctorCategory_And_PointedEndofunctors.Signature_From_ActionBased_Strength.Morphisms.FF"><span class="id" title="variable">FF</span></a></span> <span class="inlinecode"><a class="idref" href="UniMath.Semantics.LinearLogic.LinearToLinearNonLinear.html#ConstructionOfComonoidsInEilenbergMoore.xx"><span class="id" title="variable">xx</span></a></span> <span class="inlinecode"></span>.

<div class="paragraph"> </div>

  If anyone knows a way to avoid this, we would be happy to hear it! 
</div>
<div class="code">

